    "query": "How can we develop a computational model for protein-RNA binding site prediction that effectively integrates both global and local features, handles class imbalance, and produces well-calibrated predictions? Existing prediction methods typically rely on sequence or structure information and employ machine learning or deep learning techniques. They often extract features at a single scale and do not effectively combine global and local contextual information. Moreover, due to the inherent class imbalance in binding site data, these models tend to have a trade-off between precision and recall, and their confidence scores are often poorly calibrated, limiting their practical utility.",
